<h1>PC Diagnostics</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>System &gt; PC Diagnostics</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">The</span> <span class="Command">PC Diagnostics</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is destined to check the specification of your PC against the requirements of KUBE.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Call the function and a similar dialog will appear:</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../User_Interface/Menus/PCDiagnostics.gif" width="612px" height="542px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">It will contain information about your operating system, processor, memory and display properties. On the left of each information window appear different status images:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">The <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>green sign</b></span> means the checked parameter is <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>OK</b></span> for running KUBE. In this case the information window will be empty.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">The <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>yellow exclamation mark</b></span> has the signification of warning message. The meaning is: this checked parameter doesn't correspond to the KUBE requirements, but it is acceptable anyway. In this case the information window will display the minimum requirements concerning the parameter and a list of possible problems when running the KUBE software.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">The <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>red 'x' sign</b></span> indicates impossible work in KUBE. In this case the information window will show the minimum required values for this parameter to be accepted by KUBE.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>The information shown in PC Diagnostics window can be stored as a text file (click on the <span class="Button">Save</span> button) and sent to your local Partner to assist in fault-finding.</p>
